Copyright (c) 2024–2026 Ildar Vilsurovich Gaisin (Гайсин Ильдар Вильсурович) (GitHub: ildargiv) ("the Licensor").

This licence applies to the source code in this repository published on or after 2026-10-22 and to every version of KopiTehnik Print released on or after that date ("the Software"). The Software includes its source code, official builds and installers, documentation and the KopiTehnik Print name and logo, but not the third-party components described in section 11.

By installing, running, copying or building the Software you agree to this licence. If you do not agree, do not use the Software.

## 1. Definitions

- **"You"** means the individual or the organisation that uses the Software. If you use the Software for an organisation, "you" means that organisation together with every organisation that controls it, is controlled by it or is under common control with it ("affiliates"). "Control" means owning more than 50% of the voting rights or having the right to direct management.
- **"Workstation"** means one physical or virtual computer (including each virtual machine, terminal-server or remote-desktop session and container) on which the Software is installed and used to work with printers, that is, to prepare and send print jobs. It does not matter whether the Software is operated by a person or by an AI agent (including through the MCP server or the command line): what counts is the computer that works with printers. A computer or server that runs the Software only to relay commands and does not prepare or send print jobs is not a Workstation. One Workstation may be connected to any number of printers.
- **"Location"** means one physical place of business at one street address (a shop, studio, kiosk, office or home office). A mobile or event business with no fixed place counts as one Location.
- **"Commercial Use"** means any use in connection with a business, trade or profession, or for which you or anyone else is paid, including printing for customers, whether or not for profit. Use by a non-profit, school, government body or other organisation is Commercial Use unless section 2.1 applies.
- **"Personal Use"** means use by an individual for their own private, family or hobby purposes, with no payment from anyone for the result.
- **"Sheet"** means one physical sheet of paper or other media sent to a printer from the Software, as counted by the Software's print counter.
- **"Official Release"** means an installer or executable published by the Licensor on the Releases page of https://github.com/ildargiv/KopiTehnik-Print, without any change.

## 2. Free licence

Subject to this licence, the Licensor grants you a free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, worldwide licence to install, run and copy the Software:

2.1. **Personal Use** — on any number of Workstations that you own or control.

2.2. **Commercial Use on one Workstation** — on **one Workstation at one Location**, for each business (together with its affiliates).

You may also install the Software on one additional Workstation used only as a backup that does not print while the main Workstation is in use, and you may move the free licence to another Workstation or Location if you stop using it on the old one.

## 3. Paid commercial licence

You need a separate paid commercial licence from the Licensor before you:

a) use the Software for Commercial Use on more than one Workstation (other than the backup in section 2), or at more than one Location, at the same time;

b) operate as, or for, a chain, franchise or group of businesses under common brand or control, where the Software is used at more than one Location of that group (each franchisee that has only one Workstation at one Location and is a separate business may use section 2.2, unless the franchisor installs, supplies or requires the Software);

c) exceed any volume limit that applies under section 4 once such a limit is introduced;

d) provide the Software, or access to it, to other people or businesses as part of a product or service, including preinstalling it on computers or kiosks you sell or rent, offering it as a hosted or remote service, or selling, renting, sublicensing or bundling it.

There is no public price list yet. The terms of a commercial licence are agreed with the Licensor individually in a written agreement. Contact: the Licensor through the project page on GitHub (https://github.com/ildargiv/KopiTehnik-Print), for example by opening an issue or a discussion.

## 4. Possible future volume limit (notice)

4.1. At the date of this licence the Software has no limit on the number of Sheets printed. You are informed now that future versions of the Software may show a reminder about the commercial licence, and may limit the number of Sheets printed per Workstation per calendar day, for Commercial Use under section 2.2.

4.2. Any such limit will: (a) be described in the release notes of the version that introduces it and in this licence before or when that version is released; (b) not block opening, editing, saving or exporting files, and not delete or damage your files or settings; (c) not stop a print job that has already started; and (d) not apply to Personal Use.

4.3. A version of the Software that you have already installed is governed by the licence that came with it. Automatic updates will not apply a version with new or stricter limits without showing you the new licence terms first. You may keep using an earlier version under the licence that came with it.

